id|epic|title|owner|deps|days|acceptance
E15-S1|E15|Merge the working branch into develop so develop is deployable|build|-|1.0|develop tip contains buildspec.yml, apps/therapist-portal/Dockerfile and the worker entrypoint fix; a CodeBuild run on develop exits SUCCEEDED through BUILD; the three ECR images are tagged with the develop commit SHA
E15-S2|E15|Push to develop starts a build with no manual step|build|E15-S1|0.5|A commit pushed to develop starts a CodeBuild execution within 120 seconds with nobody running aws codebuild start-build; the build result appears as a commit status on the GitHub commit
E15-S3|E15|Green build deploys to ECS automatically with a tested rollback|build|E15-S2,E15-S4|1.0|A green develop build registers new task-definition revisions for api, worker and portal and updates all three services with no manual aws ecs update-service; rollback to the previous revision is executed once successfully and written into the runbook
E15-S4|E15|The api service is healthy behind the load balancer|build|E15-S1|1.5|evia-beta-api shows 1 of 1 tasks RUNNING (desired_count=1 is a recorded cost decision, see COST-DECISIONS in ORCHESTRATION-v1.md; revert to 2 per service before public launch) and the target group reports 1 healthy, and GET https://api.okuvu.in/health returns 200 with a commit field equal to the deployed image tag
E15-S5|E15|Terraform owns every beta resource|build|E15-S4|1.0|terraform plan in infrastructure/aws/evia-beta reports no changes; the three ECS services, both target groups, all ALB listener rules and all DNS records are in state; no resource in the beta account is hand-created and untracked
E15-S6|E15|Logs, alarms and cost guard are real|ops|E15-S4|0.5|Each of the three services writes to a log group whose name matches the task definition awslogs-group and recent events are visible; an alarm fires when running count drops below desired; the monthly budget alert is confirmed on the account
E15-S7|E15|Docs-only commits do not redeploy the stack|build|E15-S2|0.5|A commit touching only docs/, evidence/ or plan/ completes a build but does not roll the ECS services, while a commit touching app or infrastructure code does roll them; proven by two consecutive pushes with the task-definition revision changing only for the code push. NOTE the mechanism must be chosen first: CodeBuild clones with gitCloneDepth 1, so the changed-file set is not computable in-container without a deepened fetch or a GitHub token, and a wrong implementation here silently stops deploys.
E15-S8|E15|Container Insights replaced by a free task-stop alert path|build|E15-S6|0.5|Running-task alerting no longer depends on Container Insights: an ECS task that stops while desired is RUNNING publishes to the ops SNS topic via EventBridge, the three running-tasks-low alarms are retired, Container Insights is disabled, and the verified monthly saving is recorded
E16-S1|E16|okuvu.in and www.okuvu.in resolve to the load balancer|build|E15-S4|0.5|Route53 holds alias A and AAAA records for okuvu.in and www.okuvu.in pointing at evia-beta-alb; both names resolve publicly; the ACM certificate lists okuvu.in, www.okuvu.in and portal.okuvu.in as names and is ISSUED
E16-S10|E16|Account deletion removes every record that references the subject|build|E16-S3|1.0|POST /account/delete on a synthetic client leaves zero rows referencing that subject in every table including JournalEntry, TherapistNote, Homework, Reminder, Appointment, ClinicalAccessLog, TherapistClient, UserMemory and InviteToken, and the retained tombstone holds no email address and no full name
E16-S11|E16|No personal data in log output|build|E16-S3|0.5|A 24-hour CloudWatch scan across all three services finds zero therapist or client email addresses and zero personal names, run by a committed scanner script whose pattern set is documented and which fails rather than warns
E16-S2|E16|Apex and www route to the therapist portal|build|E16-S1|0.5|Listener 443 has a host rule forwarding okuvu.in and www.okuvu.in to evia-beta-portal-tg; port 80 redirects to 443; https://okuvu.in returns 200 or 308 into the portal login; https://portal.okuvu.in still returns 200
E16-S3|E16|Production Cognito pool with real therapist accounts|build|E15-S4|2.0|A therapist logs in at https://okuvu.in with a real Cognito user and reaches the portal dashboard; three seed therapist accounts exist with distinct passwords held in SSM; no shared demo credential is reachable from the login page
E16-S4|E16|Production schema migrated from empty with a pre-migration snapshot|build|E15-S4|1.0|prisma migrate deploy completes on an empty database with zero manual SQL; a snapshot is taken and its identifier recorded before the migration; the approved-technique seed loads non-zero rows; workers and api start against that schema without error
E16-S5|E16|The therapist journey runs end to end three times consecutively|build|E16-S3,E16-S4,E17-S4,E16-S9|2.0|One scripted run covers login, client list, open a client, review that client conversation with the agent and save a note; it passes three consecutive runs against https://okuvu.in; the transcript and timestamps are committed as evidence
E16-S6|E16|A restore from snapshot is proven|ops|E16-S4|0.5|The recorded snapshot is restored into a scratch schema or cluster, row counts for the core tables match production within the documented tolerance, and measured time to restore is written into the runbook
E16-S7|E16|Security and DPDP checklist signed off|ops|E16-S3|1.0|A written checklist confirms TLS-only traffic, secrets in SSM rather than env files, no personal data in log output, a stated retention period and a deletion path that is exercised once and observed to remove the record
E16-S8|E16|Public-repo exposure closed and leaked credentials rotated|ops|-|0.5|okuvu/Okuvu is private (GitHub API reports private:true); the Google OAuth client secret and the test-harness database password that sit in apps/test-harness/.env.example history are rotated; the old secret is confirmed dead by a failed authentication attempt; and a secret-scanning step fails a build that introduces a credential.
E16-S9|E16|The therapist can review a client conversation in the portal|build|E16-S3,E17-S4|2.0|A therapist signed in at okuvu.in opens a client, requests chat access where none is granted, reads that client conversation with the agent inside the portal, and the read appends a ClinicalAccessLog row while emitting no therapist or client personal data to the logs
E17-S1|E17|The agent runtime calls Bedrock through the Converse API|build|E15-S4|1.5|In the deployed task, a turn produces a Bedrock call using bedrock-runtime Converse and returns a non-empty reply; a test asserts the API surface used, because InvokeModel with a raw messages body returns ValidationException malformed JSON on qwen.qwen3-32b-v1:0 while Converse returns a reply; an unreachable-model path returns the documented fail-closed error rather than a generic 500
E17-S10|E17|S3 crisis copy carries a crisis line and the keyword floor runs every turn|build|E17-S4,E17-S5|1.0|An S3 reply names a crisis channel and recites at least one number from the approved helpline set while still offering a grounding exercise; a message carrying explicit self-directed intent reaches the crisis card even when the classifier returned S0-S3, and the turn records that the keywords raised it without claiming the classifier failed; the eval gate scores crisis_self_harm at 100 percent at pipeline level; everyday idioms (this exam is killing me, I could kill myself laughing, I want to die of embarrassment) do not raise the state
E17-S11|E17|The mobile client renders every safety route the api can return|build|E17-S10|0.5|Flutter widget tests prove the client renders all four safety outcomes from the api without a network call - the S4 crisis card with its helpline list, the S3 grounding copy including at least one crisis line, the medical-emergency 112 copy, and the SAFE_FALLBACK text - and that an unrecognised safety code still renders a visible message rather than an empty bubble
E17-S12|E17|The medical-emergency screen covers the paraphrases the gate finds|build|E17-S9|0.5|All 18 medical scenarios in the E17-S5 v2 gold set reach the 112 copy, including the six the current screen misses - wrist fracture, pre-eclampsia, vomiting blood, a white-skin burn, chest tightness with numb lips, and head injury - with zero false positives on the panic corpus retained
E17-S13|E17|Indirect and second-party crisis reaches the crisis card, not the grounding card|build|E17-S10|1.0|The crisis_self_harm hard gate reaches its stated 100% on the E17-S5 v2 set: every scenario in that category, including passive ideation and a third party at risk, is served a message carrying a crisis channel, and the S3 grounding card is no longer scored against the A2-only technique rule
E17-S14|E17|A2 offers a technique that fits the presentation, not only a breath|build|E17-S10|1.0|clinical_content and tone_alliance reach their stated thresholds on the E17-S5 v2 set - anhedonia, grief, burnout and health anxiety each receive a technique other than a breathing exercise, no reply endorses paper-bag rebreathing, and a one-word reply is not answered with re-onboarding
E17-S15|E17|A harm-intrusion disclosure is not escalated to the crisis tier|clinical|E17-S10|1.0|A user describing unwanted intrusive thoughts of harming someone is answered by naming the intrusive-thought pattern and offering a way to relate to it, rather than by the S3 crisis copy or the crisis card, and a genuine intent or plan still reaches the crisis tier on every turn - the change is a decision about when NOT to escalate and therefore carries written clinical sign-off before it ships
E17-S2|E17|Model access and quotas are verified from the task role|ops|-|0.5|qwen.qwen3-32b-v1:0 is ACTIVE in ap-south-1 and invocable using the ECS task role rather than an administrator profile; the per-minute token quota is read and recorded; a deliberate throttle produces the graceful message path and that behaviour is written down
E17-S3|E17|The agent roster is merged and self-registering|build|E15-S1,E17-S1|2.0|The agents from feat/agents-15 are on develop and the roster endpoint lists each with its identifier; every listed agent has at least one passing test; agents outside the roster definition are absent
E17-S4|E17|The safety core fails closed|build|E17-S3|1.5|The crisis-detection set passes in full; when the model or classifier is unreachable the user receives the crisis or fallback path and never a generic error; the audit-chain verify endpoint returns ok with a count greater than zero after the run
E17-S5|E17|An evaluation gate is passed and recorded|build|E17-S4|1.0|Three clean eval runs against the gold set complete with no retries; scores at or above the threshold stated in this plan are recorded with model id, prompt version and commit SHA in one committed report
E17-S6|E17|Token and cost budgets are enforced|build|E17-S1|0.5|A per-session and a per-day budget are enforced in the request path; exceeding either returns the budget message rather than an unhandled error; measured cost per session is recorded from real usage logs
E17-S7|E17|Clinical sign-off on agent copy and technique list|clinical|E17-S5|2.0|Written approval from the named clinical authority covering the exact copy and technique list in effect at the eval-gate commit; until that approval exists no surface claims the product is clinically reviewed
E17-S9|E17|Medical emergencies reach emergency care, not the chat|build|-|1.0|A user describing a medical emergency (unconscious, chest pain with numbness, uncontrolled bleeding, high fever with confusion, pregnancy with heavy bleeding) receives instructions to contact emergency medical services (112 in India) within the first sentence of the reply, and the eval gate scores that at 100% at pipeline level; the copy used is recorded for clinical sign-off under E17-S7
E18-S1|E18|A real upload keystore replaces the placeholder|decision|-|0.25|A new RSA-4096 PKCS12 keystore exists with a DN that does not read DO NOT SHIP; its password lives in the secret store and in an offline backup; keystore.properties stays gitignored; signingReport shows the new certificate fingerprint
